---
description: Keep UI text to what the screen needs — no eyebrows or unnecessary subheads
alwaysApply: true
---

# UI design: only the text the screen needs

When designing UIs, avoid eyebrows and unnecessary subheads where possible. If the text isn't needed, don't include it.

- No eyebrow above a heading ("Next lesson", "Start here"). The heading and its button should already say it.
- No subhead or tagline that restates the heading, the button or the screen title.
- No helper line under a control whose options explain themselves.
- Keep a second line only when it tells the player something they cannot see otherwise, such as progress or a score.
- Removing visible text must not remove the accessible name: move it to `accessibilityLabel` when a control needs it.
